ookie that was bought by the facility. As a result the child had an allergic reaction and was taken to urgent care. There were two other incidents where the allergy notification was ignored. The same child was given a snack food that contained milk. The sibling, also allergic to milk was given a product containing milk. These actions also resulted in an allergic reaction.","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026643233","violation_type_title":"Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Demonstrate Competency, Good Judgment, Self-control (26 TAC §746.1201(1))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1196022-i20220601-2-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-3301-i","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-1196022-i20220601-2","date":"2022-06-01","original_code":"746.3301(i)","severity":"medium_high","severity_label":"Medium-high risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2022-06-28","finding":"Nutrition and Food Service - Must not serve identified foods to allergic child: There were at least three incidents where a child was served food he was allergic to. The first incident a child was given a snack that had an allergy warning because it was made with milk. The second incident occurred when the same child was given a cookie that contained milk and eggs. The child is allergic to both ingredients. Another child was given a muffin made from milk. The child is allergic to milk.","topic":"health","source_record_id":"1026641451","violation_type_title":"Nutrition and Food Service - Must not serve identified foods to allergic child (26 TAC §746.3301(i))","topic_label":"Health records & medication"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-1196022-i20220601","date":"2022-06-01","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"No deficiencies cited","passed":true,"violation_count":0,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905808617","url":"https://data.texas.gov/resource/m5q4-3y3d.json?activity_id=90580861